// JavaScript implementation facet. Events are declared in input.kz (merged at
// import); this file holds the |js proc bodies.
//
// FRONTIER — this facet cannot complete, and the reason is not in this file.
// `leq-zero` is `[norun|expand]`: its body is a `~std/template:define` whose
// text is Zig (a `blk:` expression over a `union(enum)`). The [expand]
// transform runs before emission and is HOST-BLIND — it splices that Zig
// verbatim into whatever target is being emitted, so `--lang=js` produces a
// `sum_to_event` handler containing `break :blk Result{ .yes = {} }`. Supplying
// a `~proc leq-zero|js` here does not help: the proc is emitted, and then
// ignored, because the invocation was already replaced by the expansion.
//
// Fixing it needs host routing in the template registry — `define` is keyed by
// name alone, so a second `define(name: "leq-zero")` in this file would collide
// with the Zig one rather than sit beside it. That is a language-surface
// decision, not a fixture port, so this test is left honestly red for JS.

~proc print-result|js { console.log(`${value}`); }
